                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "236004827",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197963583718",
                            "num_reviews": 407,
                            "playtime_forever": 115,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 115,
                            "last_played": 1790227673
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is an interesting game. It's obviously a labor of love, and for sure it's unique. A bit of logic puzzle, a bit of minesweeper, a bit of Match 3. \nI would recommend it if:\nYou are looking for a slow, thoughtful, weighing the probabilities with each move kind of gameplay.\nYou like a cute, pixel graphics aesthetic and can tolerate a repetitive chiptune OST.\nYou are able to figure out rules without a lot of handholding.\nYou are okay with relatively long gaming sessions that can be scuttled by RNG, requiring you to start a full level over (not a full run, mind you, but an often lengthy level).\n\nI would not recommend it if:\nYou are looking for fast-paced Match 3 gameplay with endorphin-stimulating chain reactions. \nYou want a game you can play on your work laptop on your coffee breaks.\nYou failed the logic section of the GRE.\n\nUnfortunately, after 2 hours, I realized I was more in the latter of the above categories, and I've thrown in the towel, at least for the moment. But in the abstract, I understand that this isn't an awful game, and more patient and cerebral gamers may really enjoy it.",
